---
layout: layouts/identity.njk
permalink: /identity/imagery/
title: Imagery & motion
description: Photography, video and motion direction for the Teenaz Spa visual identity.
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="stack--lg stack" style="max-width: 48rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule reveal" data-reveal>Imagery &amp; motion</p>
      <h1 class="display-2 reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
        How it should <em>look and move</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="lead reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
        Photography carries more of this identity than any other element. The brief below
        is written to be handed to a photographer as-is.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── A note on the frames ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section--alt">
  <div class="shell shell--narrow">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card__body">
        <p class="eyebrow">About the frames on these pages</p>
        <p class="card__text">
          Every image area in this system is currently a painted field, not a photograph.
          Each one is a soft, out-of-focus wash in the brand's warm grade — enough to show
          how the palette behaves at image scale, how type sits on a scrim and how a grid
          of pictures reads together, without asserting a photograph that has not been
          taken. They are sized and toned to be swapped one-for-one with the real shots.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Tonal range ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="tone-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">01 — Grade</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="tone-t">One warm grade, six registers</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        Every photograph is graded to the same warm neutral. Highlights lean ivory,
        shadows lean espresso, and nothing in the library is allowed to go cool. Within
        that single grade, six registers give a gallery variety without breaking the set.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="grid-3">
      {% set tones = [
        ['warm', 'Warm', 'Towels, fabric, skin. The default register.'],
        ['bronze', 'Bronze', 'Oils, brass, candlelight. The warmest end.'],
        ['steam', 'Steam', 'Water, steam, wet stone. The lightest register.'],
        ['stone', 'Stone', 'Marble, plaster, rough surfaces.'],
        ['sage', 'Sage', 'Plants and the few cooler moments allowed.'],
        ['deep', 'Deep', 'Low-lit rooms. Only where type sits over the image.']
      ] %}
      {% for tone in tones %}
      <figure class="figure reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="{{ loop.index }}">
        <div class="figure__frame" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;">
          <canvas data-media="tone-{{ tone[0] }}" data-tone="{{ tone[0] }}" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="figure__caption">
          <strong style="color: var(--text);">{{ tone[1] }}</strong> — {{ tone[2] }}
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Treatment ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section--raised" aria-labelledby="treat-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">02 — Treatment</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="treat-t">Six rules that make the set cohere</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="grid-3">
      {% for rule in identity.imagery.treatment %}
      <div class="card card--sand reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="{{ loop.index }}">
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="h4">{{ rule.name }}</p>
          <p class="card__text">{{ rule.note }}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Subjects ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="subject-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">03 — Subjects</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="subject-t">What to photograph, and what to refuse</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        The subject list leans towards sensory detail rather than people looking at the
        camera. Close, quiet, specific. When a person appears they are mid-gesture and
        respectfully covered.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="do-dont">
      <div class="do-dont__col do-dont__col--do reveal" data-reveal>
        <p class="do-dont__title">Shoot</p>
        <ul class="do-dont__list">
          {% for subject in identity.imagery.subjects %}<li>{{ subject }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="do-dont__col do-dont__col--dont reveal" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
        <p class="do-dont__title">Never</p>
        <ul class="do-dont__list">
          {% for item in identity.imagery.avoid %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Text over image ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section--alt" aria-labelledby="scrim-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">04 — Type over photography</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="scrim-t">Never trust the picture alone</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        A photograph that is dark enough for white type today will be replaced by one that
        is not. Text over an image always sits on a scrim, so legibility is a property of
        the system rather than of the particular shot.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <figure class="figure">
        <div class="overlay-media" style="border-radius: var(--r-lg);">
          <canvas data-media="scrim-with" data-tone="warm" aria-hidden="true" style="position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;"></canvas>
          <span class="overlay-media__scrim"></span>
          <div class="overlay-media__content" style="min-height: 20rem; padding: var(--s-6);">
            <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--on-deep">With scrim</p>
            <p class="h2" style="color: var(--ivory);">{{ identity.placeholder.short }}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="figure__caption">Correct. Ivory type holds at AA over any frame in the library.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="figure">
        <div class="overlay-media" style="border-radius: var(--r-lg);">
          <canvas data-media="scrim-with" data-tone="warm" aria-hidden="true" style="position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%;"></canvas>
          <div class="overlay-media__content" style="min-height: 20rem; padding: var(--s-6);">
            <p class="eyebrow" style="color: rgba(247,242,234,0.8);">No scrim</p>
            <p class="h2" style="color: var(--ivory);">{{ identity.placeholder.short }}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="figure__caption">Wrong. The same type on the same frame, now unreadable in the light areas.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Video ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="video-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">05 — Video</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="video-t">Background video, held still</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="split" style="align-items: start;">
      <div class="media-band reveal ken" data-reveal>
        <div class="media-band__frame" style="border-radius: var(--r-lg); overflow: hidden;">
          <canvas data-media="video-frame" data-tone="steam" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="do-dont__list" style="font-size: var(--t-body);">
        {% for rule in identity.imagery.video %}<li>{{ rule }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Motion ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section--raised" id="motion" aria-labelledby="motion-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">06 — Motion</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="motion-t">Slow enough to be calming</h2>
      <p class="body-text">
        Four durations, one easing curve. Everything on these pages already uses them —
        the sections you have scrolled past rose into place at 900ms. Motion supports the
        atmosphere and never asks for attention.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="spec" style="margin-bottom: var(--s-8);">
      {% for m in identity.motion %}
      <div style="display: grid; gap: var(--s-2); padding-block: var(--s-4); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-quiet);">
        <div class="scale-row__meta">
          <span><strong style="color: var(--text);">{{ m.name }}</strong></span>
          <span><code>{{ m.token }}</code></span>
          <span>{{ m.value }}</span>
          <span>{{ m.curve }}</span>
        </div>
        <p class="spec__note">{{ m.note }}</p>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="do-dont">
      <div class="do-dont__col do-dont__col--do">
        <p class="do-dont__title">Use</p>
        <ul class="do-dont__list">
          <li>Gentle fade with an upward rise</li>
          <li>Slow image scaling on load</li>
          <li>Soft parallax, small displacement only</li>
          <li>Smooth colour transitions on hover</li>
          <li>Slow gallery cross-fades</li>
          <li>Seamless, muted background video</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="do-dont__col do-dont__col--dont">
        <p class="do-dont__title">Never</p>
        <ul class="do-dont__list">
          <li>Fast or snapping animation</li>
          <li>Bouncing or elastic easing</li>
          <li>Scroll-jacking or pinned sections</li>
          <li>Cursor followers and custom cursors</li>
          <li>Flashing or high-contrast transitions</li>
          <li>Large rotating carousels</li>
          <li>Autoplay audio, ever</li>
          <li>Animating every element on a page</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card card--sand" style="margin-top: var(--s-7);">
      <div class="card__body">
        <p class="h4">Reduced motion</p>
        <p class="card__text">
          Under <code>prefers-reduced-motion: reduce</code> every transition and animation
          collapses to 0.01ms, reveals start visible, the floating button is shown without
          sliding, and background video is replaced by its poster frame. Nothing becomes
          unreachable and no content depends on motion to appear.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Responsive & accessibility ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section" id="quality" aria-labelledby="quality-t">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="section-head section-head--wide">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-rule">07 — Quality floor</p>
      <h2 class="h1" id="quality-t">What every page must clear</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="h4">Responsive</p>
          <ul class="do-dont__list" style="font-size: var(--t-small);">
            <li>Spacing stays generous on mobile — the scale shrinks, the rhythm does not</li>
            <li>Body text never below 16px; small text never below 14px</li>
            <li>Touch targets at least 44px, buttons 48px</li>
            <li>Sections stack in reading order</li>
            <li>No horizontal overflow at any width</li>
            <li>Images re-crop rather than letterbox</li>
            <li>One idea per viewport, on every screen size</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="card__body">
          <p class="h4">Accessible</p>
          <ul class="do-dont__list" style="font-size: var(--t-small);">
            <li>Body text at AA or better against its background</li>
            <li>Bronze and sage restricted to large text, icons and borders</li>
            <li>Focus is always visible, and additive to the resting border</li>
            <li>Text over photography always on a scrim</li>
            <li>Form labels visible, never placeholder-only</li>
            <li>Reduced motion fully honoured</li>
            <li>Every image carries alt text written for its content</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
